      "text": "To color the rows in an alternating fashion while using `\\multirow`, you need the `xcolor` package with the `table` option.\n\nThere are two main ways to do this depending on your goal:\n1.  **Zebra Striping (Row-by-row):** Best for following a single line from \"Dependency\" to \"Effect.\"\n2.  **Block Coloring:** Best for grouping all dependencies of a single \"Metabolite\" together.\n\n### Option 1: Zebra Striping (Line-by-Line)\nThis is the most effective way to link a dependency to its effect. We use `\\rowcolors` to automate the alternating colors.\n\n**Note:** When using colors with `\\multirow`, the background color can \"cover\" the text. To fix this, we wrap the metabolite name in a `\\cellcolor{white}`.\n\n```latex\n\\documentclass{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{multirow}\n\\usepackage[table]{xcolor} % Required for coloring\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Glycolysis ODE Metabolite Dependencies}\n\\label{tab:glycolysis-dependencies}\n% This command starts alternating colors from the 2nd row (header is row 1)\n\\rowcolors{2}{gray!10}{white} \n\\begin{tabular}{|l|l|c|}\n\\hline\n\\rowcolor{gray!30} \\textbf{Metabolite} \u0026 \\textbf{Dependency} \u0026 \\textbf{Effect} \\\\\n\\hline\nGLC (Intracellular Glucose) \u0026 GLC \u0026 $\\pm$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 GLC \u0026 + \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 G6P \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\multirow{-3}{*}{\\cellcolor{white}G6P} \u0026 F6P \u0026 + (via GPI equilibrium) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 G6P \u0026 + \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\multirow{-2}{*}{\\cellcolor{white}F6P} \u0026 F6P \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 F6P \u0026 + \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\multirow{-2}{*}{\\cellcolor{white}F16BP} \u0026 F16BP \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 F16BP \u0026 + \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 3PG \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\multirow{-3}{*}{\\cellcolor{white}3PG} \u0026 PEP \u0026 + (via ENO equilibrium) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 3PG \u0026 + \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 PEP \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\multirow{-3}{*}{\\cellcolor{white}PEP} \u0026 F16BP \u0026 $-$ (allosteric activation of PK) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\cellcolor{white} \u0026 PEP \u0026 + \\\\\n\\cline{2-3}\n\\multirow{-2}{*}{\\cellcolor{white}Pyruvate} \u0026 F16BP \u0026 + (allosteric activation of PK) \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\\end{document}\n```\n\n### Key adjustments made:\n1.  **`\\rowcolors{2}{gray!10}{white}`**: Automatically colors every other row light gray starting from the second row of the table.\n2.  **`\\cellcolor{white}`**: Applied to the first column cells. This prevents the \"Zebra\" stripes from cutting through the middle of your Metabolite names, keeping that column clean.\n3.  **`\\multirow` position**: I moved the `\\multirow` to the *bottom* row of each group using a negative number (e.g., `\\multirow{-3}{*}{...}`). In LaTeX, coloring a row *after* a multirow is declared often covers the text. Placing it at the end of the group ensures the text sits \"on top\" of the colors.\n4.  **`\\cline{2-3}`**: Used instead of `\\hline` inside a group so that the horizontal line doesn\u0027t strike through your \"Metabolite\" name in the first column.\n\n---\n\n### Pro-Tip: A Cleaner \"Professional\" Version\nIf you want the table to look more modern and readable, it is often recommended to remove the vertical lines and use the `booktabs` package. Here is how that looks with subtle shading:\n\n```latex\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage[table]{xcolor}\n\n...\n\n\\begin{tabular}{llc}\n\\toprule\n\\rowcolor{gray!20} \\textbf{Metabolite} \u0026 \\textbf{Dependency} \u0026 \\textbf{Effect} \\\\\n\\midrule\nGLC \u0026 GLC \u0026 $\\pm$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\addlinespace\n\\rowcolor{gray!5} \u0026 GLC \u0026 + \\\\\n\\rowcolor{gray!5} \u0026 G6P \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\rowcolor{gray!5} \\multirow{-3}{*}{G6P} \u0026 F6P \u0026 + (via GPI equilibrium) \\\\\n\\addlinespace\n\u0026 G6P \u0026 + \\\\\n\\multirow{-2}{*}{F6P} \u0026 F6P \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\addlinespace\n\\rowcolor{gray!5} \u0026 F6P \u0026 + \\\\\n\\rowcolor{gray!5} \\multirow{-2}{*}{F16BP} \u0026 F16BP \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n```\n*This style uses `\\addlinespace` to separate metabolites and `\\rowcolor` to highlight the even-numbered groups.*",
