        "text": "To achieve a professional `booktabs` look with alternating colors for individual rows (dependencies and effects) while keeping the metabolite column clean, the most robust method is using the **`nicematrix"
      }, {
        "text": "`** package. \n\nUnlike the standard `tabular` environment, `nicematrix` is designed to handle colors"
      }, {
        "text": " and `booktabs` rules without the common \"white line\" glitches or text-overlapping issues.\n\n### The Recommended"
      }, {
        "text": " Solution: `nicematrix`\nThis approach allows you to define the row coloring in a single \"pre-code"
      }, {
        "text": "\" block. To keep the metabolite column white, we simply use a `\\Block` with a white background.\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "```latex\n\\documentclass{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\\usepackage{nicematrix} % Modern table package\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\"
      }, {
        "text": "begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Glycolysis ODE Metabolite Dependencies}\n\\label"
      }, {
        "text": "{tab:glycolysis-dependencies}\n% Standard row height adjustment for clarity\n\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1"
      }, {
        "text": ".2} \n\\begin{NiceTabular}{llc}[\n    % Color rows starting from the "
      }, {
        "text": "2nd row (index 2)\n    code-before \u003d \\rowcolors{2}{gray!10}{white}"
      }, {
        "text": "\n]\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Metabolite} \u0026 \\textbf{Dependency} \u0026 \\textbf{Effect"
      }, {
        "text": "} \\\\\n\\midrule\n% \\Block{rows-cols}{text} automatically centers and prevents row coloring from overlapping\n"
      }, {
        "text": "\\Block{1-1}{GLC (Intracellular Glucose)} \u0026 GLC \u0026 $\\pm$ (self-limiting) \\\\"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{3-1}{G6P (Glucose-6-Phosphate)} \n    \u0026 GLC"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 G6P \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n    \u0026 F6P \u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " + (via GPI equilibrium) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{2-1}{F6P (Fructose"
      }, {
        "text": "-6-Phosphate)} \n    \u0026 G6P \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 F6P \u0026 $-$"
      }, {
        "text": " (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{2-1}{F16BP (Fructose"
      }, {
        "text": "-1,6-Bisphosphate)} \n    \u0026 F6P \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 F16"
      }, {
        "text": "BP \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{3-1}{3PG (3"
      }, {
        "text": "-Phosphoglycerate)} \n    \u0026 F16BP \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 3PG \u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n    \u0026 PEP \u0026 + (via ENO equilibrium) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\"
      }, {
        "text": "Block{3-1}{PEP (Phosphoenolpyruvate)} \n    \u0026 3PG \u0026 + \\\\"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    \u0026 PEP \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n    \u0026 F16BP \u0026 $-$ (alloster"
      }, {
        "text": "ic activation of PK) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{2-1}{Pyruvate} \n    \u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " PEP \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 F16BP \u0026 + (allosteric activation of PK) \\\\\n\\"
      }, {
        "text": "bottomrule\n\\end{NiceTabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\\end{document}\n"
      }, {
        "text": "```\n\n### Why this works:\n1.  **`code-before \u003d \\rowcolors{2}{gray!1"
      }, {
        "text": "0}{white}`**: This handles the alternating colors globally. You don\u0027t have to manually label every row.\n2."
      }, {
        "text": "  **`\\Block{rows-cols}{text}`**: This is the `nicematrix` equivalent of `\\multirow`."
      }, {
        "text": " It is superior because it naturally sits *on top* of the background colors and automatically stays white if the block spans multiple rows ("
      }, {
        "text": "effectively \"blocking\" out the zebra stripes for the Metabolite name).\n3.  **`booktabs` compatibility**: "
      }, {
        "text": "`nicematrix` understands `\\toprule`, `\\midrule`, and `\\bottomrule` and ensures the background colors"
      }, {
        "text": " stop exactly at the rules.\n\n---\n\n### Alternative: Traditional `xcolor` + `booktabs`\nIf you cannot"
      }, {
        "text": " use `nicematrix`, you can achieve this with standard tools by setting the rules\u0027 padding to zero (to avoid"
      }, {
        "text": " white gaps) and using `\\cellcolor{white}` for the first column.\n\n```latex\n\\documentclass{article"
      }, {
        "text": "}\n\\usepackage{multirow}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage[table]{xcolor}\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "\\begin{document}\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Glycolysis ODE Metabolite"
      }, {
        "text": " Dependencies}\n% Fix for booktabs + colors (removes white gap around rules)\n\\setlength{\\aboverulesep"
