      "text": "To keep the first column (Metabolite) clear while alternating colors only for the \"Dependency\" and \"Effect\" columns, you can use the `cols` key within the `\\rowcolors` command inside `nicematrix`.\n\nThis is the cleanest method because it allows you to define the color logic once at the top, rather than coloring every individual cell.\n\n```latex\n\\documentclass{article}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{nicematrix}\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\caption{Glycolysis ODE Metabolite Dependencies}\n\\label{tab:glycolysis-dependencies}\n\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1.3} % Better spacing for readability\n\\begin{NiceTabular}{llc}[\n    code-before \u003d {\n        % This tells LaTeX: Start at row 2, alternate gray and white, \n        % but only apply it to columns 2 and 3.\n        \\rowcolors{2}{gray!10}{white}[cols\u003d{2-3}]\n    }\n]\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Metabolite} \u0026 \\textbf{Dependency} \u0026 \\textbf{Effect} \\\\\n\\midrule\n\nGLC (Intracellular Glucose) \u0026 GLC \u0026 $\\pm$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{3-1}{G6P (Glucose-6-Phosphate)} \n    \u0026 GLC \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 G6P \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n    \u0026 F6P \u0026 + (via GPI equilibrium) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{2-1}{F6P (Fructose-6-Phosphate)} \n    \u0026 G6P \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 F6P \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{2-1}{F16BP (Fructose-1,6-Bisphosphate)} \n    \u0026 F6P \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 F16BP \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{3-1}{3PG (3-Phosphoglycerate)} \n    \u0026 F16BP \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 3PG \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n    \u0026 PEP \u0026 + (via ENO equilibrium) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{3-1}{PEP (Phosphoenolpyruvate)} \n    \u0026 3PG \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 PEP \u0026 $-$ (self-limiting) \\\\\n    \u0026 F16BP \u0026 $-$ (allosteric activation of PK) \\\\\n\\midrule\n\n\\Block{2-1}{Pyruvate} \n    \u0026 PEP \u0026 + \\\\\n    \u0026 F16BP \u0026 + (allosteric activation of PK) \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{NiceTabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\\end{document}\n```\n\n### Why this is the best solution:\n1.  **`cols\u003d{2-3}`**: This specific parameter inside `\\rowcolors` restricts the background paint to only the columns you want. The \"Metabolite\" column remains whatever the default table background is (usually white/transparent).\n2.  **`\\Block{n-1}{...}`**: Because we are using `nicematrix`, the `\\Block` command automatically handles the vertical centering of your metabolite names without you having to worry about `multirow` math or text being covered by row colors.\n3.  **No Vertical Lines**: Following `booktabs` principles, this relies on horizontal rules and subtle shading to guide the eye, which is much easier to read for scientific data.\n4.  **Row Height**: I added `\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1.3}`. When using background colors, adding a little extra \"breathing room\" prevents the text from looking cramped against the color boundaries.\n\n**Note:** You may need to compile your LaTeX document **twice** the first time you use `nicematrix` so it can calculate the positions of the background blocks correctly.",
